The general framework is one layer of the spiral at a time, given by layer running from 0 to the ceiling of half the smaller dimension (width or height). At each layer:

- A top row is collected from the left edge to the right edge (grid[layer][layer] to grid[layer][w-layer-1]).
- A right column is collected from the row after the layer to the row before the bottom (since the top row already included the corner at grid[layer][w-layer-1]).
- The bottom row is collected backwards only when the layer is not already the bottom row, so that the corner at grid[h-layer-1][w-layer-1] is appended once and only once.
- The left column is collected backwards only when the layer is not already the leftmost column, likewise to avoid a duplicate corner.

